---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Panel from "../components/Panel.astro";

/*
 * Etap 1.12, before registration opens: the operator is named here only as
 * akApp Studio. Under an unregistered business (NDG) the service provider is
 * a natural person, so add the full name and address to section 1, and the
 * same in privacy.astro.
 */
---
<Base
  title="Terms of Service · Xebeka"
  description="The terms of Xebeka, the online RPG played in the browser, including the rules of play."
>
  <Panel title="Terms of Service">
    <article class="prose">
      <p class="doc__date">Last updated 27 September 2026</p>
      <p>
        These terms apply to Xebeka, the online role-playing game at xebeka.com, and to your
        account in it. By creating an account you agree to them, so please read them first. They
        include the rules of play, which keep the game fair for everyone. How we handle your data
        is described in the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>1. Who runs Xebeka</h3>
      <p>
        Xebeka is run by <a href="https://akappstudio.pl">akApp Studio</a>. You can reach us at
        <a href="mailto:kontakt@xebeka.com">kontakt@xebeka.com</a>, the address for everything
        these terms mention: questions, reports and complaints.
      </p>

      <h3>2. A game still being built</h3>
      <p>
        Xebeka is in beta. Creatures, items, maps and balance change as the game grows, and the
        game may be unavailable for a while when it is updated. During the beta, characters and
        their progress may be reset, in particular when the game moves to a new server. Whenever we
        can, we announce a reset on this site before it happens.
      </p>

      <h3>3. What you need</h3>
      <p>
        A current web browser with JavaScript turned on, on a computer or a phone, and an internet
        connection. There is nothing to install.
      </p>

      <h3>4. Your account</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          You must be at least 13 years old to create an account. If you are under 18, read these
          terms together with a parent or guardian.
        </li>
        <li>
          You create an account with an email address and a password, or with a Google account.
          The agreement between us starts when you create it and lasts until it is deleted.
        </li>
        <li>Keep your password to yourself. You are responsible for what happens on your account.</li>
        <li>An account is personal. Do not sell it, share it or give it to someone else.</li>
        <li>
          You can delete your account at any time in Manage account. This removes the account and
          all its characters for good.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>5. Characters</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>An account holds up to five characters.</li>
        <li>
          A name is 3 to 20 letters (A to Z), in up to three words. It must not be offensive,
          pretend to be staff, or copy the name of a creature or of a character in the game. We may
          change or remove a name that breaks this rule.
        </li>
        <li>
          A character you delete is removed 7 days later. Until then you can change your mind and
          cancel the deletion.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3 id="rules">6. Rules of play</h3>
      <p>Xebeka is a shared world. These rules keep it fair:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Play yourself.</strong> No bots, macros or programs that play for you, no
          modified game files, and no tampering with the game's data or its connection.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Report bugs instead of using them.</strong> If you find a way to gain an
          advantage the game did not intend, tell us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Respect other players.</strong> No harassment, threats or hate speech, and no
          sharing anyone's personal information.
        </li>
        <li><strong>No scams.</strong> Do not trick other players out of their items or accounts.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>No real-money trading.</strong> Do not buy or sell characters, items or gold for
          real money.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Do not pretend to be staff.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Nothing unlawful.</strong> Do not post or send unlawful content through the game.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Fighting other players is part of the game from level 10 and does not by itself break
        these rules.
      </p>

      <h3>7. When the rules are broken</h3>
      <p>
        We may warn you, suspend your account for a time, or delete it, depending on how serious
        the breach is and whether it is repeated. If you think we got it wrong, write to us and we
        will look at it again.
      </p>

      <h3>8. Price</h3>
      <p>
        Xebeka is free to play. If optional paid features are added later, their price and terms
        will be shown before you can buy them.
      </p>

      <h3>9. The game and its content</h3>
      <p>
        The game, its code and its art belong to us or to the artists who licensed their work
        (see <a href="/credits/">Credits</a>). You get a personal right to play. Characters and
        items exist only inside the game and are not your property.
      </p>

      <h3>10. Our responsibility</h3>
      <p>
        We work to keep Xebeka running and your progress safe, but during the beta we cannot
        promise that the game will always be available, that it is free of errors, or that
        progress will never be lost or reset. Nothing in these terms limits liability that the law
        does not allow to be limited, or takes away your rights as a consumer.
      </p>

      <h3>11. Complaints</h3>
      <p>
        If something does not work as it should, write to
        <a href="mailto:kontakt@xebeka.com">kontakt@xebeka.com</a> with the email address of your
        account and a description of the problem. We answer within 14 days.
      </p>

      <h3>12. Changes to these terms</h3>
      <p>
        We may change these terms as the game develops, for example when new features arrive, and
        we announce significant changes on this site before they take effect. If you do not agree
        with a change, you can delete your account. If you keep playing after it takes effect, the
        new terms apply to you.
      </p>

      <h3>13. Law</h3>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by Polish law. If you play as a consumer, you also keep the
        protection that the law of the country where you live gives you.
      </p>
    </article>
  </Panel>
</Base>
